WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:04.600
The Griffin fought Division 2
and destroyed Ota's Labor...

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.680
before escaping back to
the Tsuchiura research labs.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.310
But the Division Manager of
Shaft Japan got cold feet...

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.610
and called in Shaft's
security division.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.940
Three-S was ordered to capture
Utsumi and take the Griffin.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.870
But Utsumi escaped
and headed for Tokyo.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.950
With him were Bud,
Kurosaki, and the Griffin.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.750
Three-S planned an ambush
at the Babylon Castle Gate.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.550
Division 2 was also
waiting, near Kawasaki.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.340
But the Griffin came
ashore on the far side...

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.050
and now Division 2 is
rushing to the scene.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.060
Tonight I'll fight to the bitter end.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:56.190
Battle At Castle Gate

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.030
Yes, we're over the Kisarazu side.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.620
Kawasaki is a land route;
boats can't go through.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.990
What? You have a live relay
to the Chiba station? Roger.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.840
Back off, small fry.
You're just going to get hurt.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.480
I only want the Ingram.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.380
So where's the Ingram?

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.280
Jet Stream Attack!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.320
Shut up!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.250
But I practiced so hard!

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.150
The station wants a voice-over, too.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.820
Voice? They want me to do reporting?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.660
Just fill in until the ground unit arrives.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.540
But...

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.870
This is being sent across the country!

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.750
Five, four, three...

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:27.090
As you can see, the Black Labor
is at the Castle Gate of Babylon.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.800
This is NO Hollywood movie!

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.680
These events are real,
coming to you live!

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:37.190
The Black Labor first appeared
at the Labor Show in Haruumi.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:42.730
After defeating Special Vehicles,
Second Section, it flew away!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:48.610
It was reported to
have crashed in Chiba...

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:52.410
but as you can see,
the Black Labor still lives!

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.060
Where did this Black
Labor come from?

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.310
Who created it, and
for what nefarious purpose?

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.310
These questions are
still shrouded in mystery.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:27.030
You are watching live
images from the scene.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:30.160
This Black Labor may
belong to a security company.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.540
It has just destroyed three other Labors...

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.910
and it's now walking around leisurely.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.510
Now it's moving toward Kawasaki.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.760
Will it slip into the sea?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:54.470
Or will it take to the skies again
to menace Tokyo?

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.350
Wait a moment!

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:12.990
It's Second Section!
A lone Ingram has appeared.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.660
The famous 98AV cuts
a brave and striking figure!

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:21.040
Your rampage is over!
You're under arrest for triggering a riot...

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.330
destruction of property,
and many other violations!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.260
I know that voice!

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:30.670
Freeze!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.990
I can't exploit a wounded man.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.450
Really, the injury isn't that bad!

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.610
Then you'll recover quickly.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.700
But...

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.620
Captain, Division 1 is ready!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:00.370
Good.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.120
I'm coming, too!

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:07.750
Officer Shinohara,
I'm not your commander.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:11.590
If you're needed,
your Captain will send for you.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:18.470
I've fought the Black Labor.
You could use that experience.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.100
Yes, but the brass hates officers...

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.190
who leave their post to
follow a personal grudge.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.440
Really?

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.400
Division 2 has no discipline.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.400
Move out!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.960
You look hard at work.
I thought you were ordered to rest up.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.420
I don't want to hear it!

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.840
Well, perhaps it was just a rumor.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.640
So, you're interested in her battle?

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.810
Why wouldn't I be?

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:09.060
I need to fly in a reserve battery.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.650
Want to tag along?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.900
Of course!

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.280
Load it up!

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.050
It's a stand-off.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:43.220
Noa, shoot! You have
to take the initiative!

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:47.190
Miss Izumi wouldn't fire
unless it was life or death.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:51.270
Sometimes I wonder
if she'd even fire then.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.230
If she doesn't fire,
the gun is useless.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:02.910
We can't let the Griffin be captured.
We have to blow it up!

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.160
More police are arriving
on the Kisarazu side.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.670
We may not be able to
reach the Griffin in our pursuit cars.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:15.800
If you have to, use the Abraham.
Machine 2 is still in good shape.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.390
Stop!

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:36.780
Hurry! Hurry! That helicopter
is stealing my best lines!

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.240
There they are!

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.490
I want to be right next to them!

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.710
What was that car?

00:10:54.960 --> 00:11:00.380
Let them go. Any battlefield
chaos will make our job easier.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.720
The Griffin's moving!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:06.600
Halt!

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.360
Noa, what are you doing?

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.150
There are people under the Griffin!

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.740
Such tremendous power!

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.870
Shouldn't we back up?
Isn't this dangerous?

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:33.250
What? Would Robert Cappa
or Cartaier Bresson back off?

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.290
Yeah, tough call.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.170
Pulitzer, here I come!

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.600
<i>I can't use the shotgun with</i>
<i>people in the line of fire.</i>

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.390
<i>What should I do?</i>
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:13.210
He's approaching from your left!

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.460
This side...

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:49.410
I didn't mean to shoot!
I didn't mean to shoot!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.540
Jesus!

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:59.090
Izumi, a loaded riot gun isn't
very well suited for swordplay.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.300
It won't happen again!
I've had enough!

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:05.510
Officer Shinshi, take over.
I'm going to evacuate the civilians.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:14.140
Abraham: Next time the
Griffin stops, move in on it.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.100
Plant the explosives on its back.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:23.070
The rest of you, board the
<i>Sangria</i> and find Utsumi.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.990
Well, Chief?

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:33.950
Shall we be going?

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:47.340
Nice gun! But you won't use it,
so I have nothing to fear.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.400
The Griffin is operating
right on the edge.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.570
Yeah, but look how well it moves.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.780
We can't capture it unless
we capture Utsumi first.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.990
It's no good.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:12.620
What's wrong?

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:18.000
They won't let us on until we
get the Far East Manager's approval.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.170
Are they trying to
make fun of the Three-S?

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.380
You want to talk to them?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.250
You better believe it!

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.510
Stupid terrorists.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.720
Hey, you can't leave your post!

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:37.810
Where are you going?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.190
Thataway.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:39.850
Thataway?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:40.850
Thataway!

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:48.190
Sorry to saddle you with
the chauffeur duties.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:51.360
I'll do whatever it takes
to save my skin!

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.240
I'll drive, eat garbage,
whatever it takes!

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:24.610
Move back! Retreat! Retreat!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.120
Good!

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:52.430
You monster!

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:11.490
What's wrong with her?
Why doesn't she use the riot gun?

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.990
Ota! Ota!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:13.950
What?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.740
Give me a hand!
I can't hold this by myself!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:23.750
Ota, come help! TV reporters
are in the way at the fight scene!

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.960
Is that why Izumi won't fire?

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:26.630
Hurry!

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.010
Ota!

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.650
Captain, what's going on?

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:50.820
It's you.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.110
Don't give me that!

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.150
This looks bad.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:58.990
The Ingram is actually doing
pretty well, considering.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:05.000
Captain, we've got the reporters.
Ota is persuading them to leave.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.670
Persuasion complete.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:09.540
The area is clear.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.420
Roger. Izumi, did you copy?

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.630
You're clear to fire.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.260
I don't enjoy saying this:

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:25.440
Freeze! One move, and I'll shoot.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.770
Coward!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.230
Step down from your machine.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:47.620
Captain, another Labor is
moving in from behind!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.000
Don't stand behind my target!

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.640
Stop, or I'll shoot!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.190
It's coming!

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.920
What happened?

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.590
Thanks, Three-S.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.520
Izumi, your opponent is
still moving. Finish him.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.310
Get up! What's wrong, Izumi?

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:51.350
Noa, answer me!

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:01.660
<i>Huh?</i>

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.580
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:18.720
<i>I'm going for the basket.</i>

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:31.640
Noa!

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:33.020
Izumi, what are you doing?

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:39.570
<i>What AM I doing?</i>
<i>They're really shouting at me.</i>

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.440
<i>It's over.</i>

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:19.650
Did you give it your best shot?

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:31.080
<i>That's what I told myself.</i>
<i>Just another few inches...</i>

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:38.090
<i>Would I have kept going?</i>
<i>Did I really give it my best?</i>

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:47.350
Noa, are you asleep?
This is no time to pass out!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:52.270
Your opponent is already up! Get up!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.060
What exploded?

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.110
Well, I'll make up for it now!

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:07.070
How many hours have
I been unconscious?

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:10.240
If it had been hours, you'd be dead!

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:13.290
You'd have been dead
in the first minute!

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.920
Fight now! You can faint later!

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.000
You could be a little nicer to me.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.960
I'm bleeding.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:24.920
What? Where did he get you?
Are you all right?

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.720
I cut my lip.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.260
You idiot!

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.140
Calm down.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:32.720
Asuma, you're right.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:36.560
If you ever said anything
nice to me, I'd go soft.

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:42.280
Look, it's not like I was
overly worried about you...

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:46.240
I just want you to fulfill
your duties, and, uh...

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.200
What are you babbling about?

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:53.120
We'll see who faints when I'm done!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:22:01.710
Ogasawara, Haruumi, and here...
why can't we stop her?

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.510
What does it take to stop this lady?

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:12.720
<i>He continues to</i>
<i>attack furiously.</i>

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:16.850
<i>He's an incredible opponent...</i>
<i>but I can take him.</i>

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:24.820
You lose!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:26.110
The only loser here...

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:32.280
IS YOU!

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:47.220
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:50.930
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:57.180
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:06.690
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:09.610
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:14.200
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:18.870
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:21.710
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:25.880
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:32.390
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:37.640
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:40.180
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:40.180 --> 00:23:43.400
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:43.650 --> 00:23:47.480
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:53.660
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:59.700
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:06.340
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:11.050
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:11.050
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:20.890 --> 00:24:25.400
Noa starts fighting back. Go get
'em Noa!! Kick his butt Alphonse!

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:28.770
One more hit... almost there!
I'll never let them get away with this.

00:24:28.820 --> 00:24:32.110
I'm gonna make them pay!
I'm counting on you Alphonse!

00:24:32.110 --> 00:24:38.120
Can Noa catch up with Griffon in time?
Will Kanuka expose 3S's sinister plots?

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:41.870
Next episode: Griffin Down!
Target Locked On!

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:46.710
Next episode

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:46.710
Griffin Down!
